{
  "name": "@link-foundation/ui-components",
  "version": "0.0.0",
  "description": "Components of the associative UI framework written in Links Notation: basic controls (button, text, number and colour fields, checkbox, radio group, switch, slider, select, combobox, progress as a bar or a ring, badge, avatar, chip, accordion) on native elements with WAI-ARIA keyboard behaviour, their stories and catalog, behaviour state machines in LiNo with a DOM-free interpreter, an actions registry that never evaluates code, DOM accessibility helpers (focus trap, roving tabindex, typeahead, key bindings, live region), charts described with the grammar of Vega-Lite (data, mark, encoding), rendered as deterministic SVG with d3-scale and d3-shape, with an accessible table twin and an optional lazy ECharts adapter, diagrams described in LiNo (flowchart, state, sequence, class), laid out by Dagre or a layout plugin, rendered as accessible SVG, exported to Mermaid text or rendered by a lazily loaded Mermaid adapter, layout elements (stack, grid, split, tab-group, dock, window, app-shell, container, paper, card, app-bar) rendered by ui-dom with a layer manager and dock layouts saved as Links Notation, a public-domain icon set, the ui-icon element and adapters for Lucide, Tabler and Material Symbols that emit asset records, and link-view, one link drawn from links-visuals geometry with shared SVG and Canvas markers, per-instance zoom and pan, and an idle-free animator",
